    ],
    "text": "Despite the admission made with regard to the identity of the subject matter, half way through the evidence of the plaintiff-appellant, upon discovering that the second amended plaint contained no schedule, the learned counsel of the plaintiff-appellant moved for an amendment of the plaint to which application the learned counsel for the defendants objected and thereafter the application for amendment of plaint was set down for order. By order dated 22.8.1996 the learned district judge having disallowed the application to amend the plaint based on the ground of laches on the part of the plaintiff-appellant dismissed his action. The present appeal has been preferred by the plaintiff-appellant, challenging the validity of the said order of dismissal and to have the matter sent back to the court exercising original jurisdiction to hear and conclude the same.",
